hly even game. Black held a +2.4 lead after move 14, then threw it away with H3 (10.0 points lost) and G5 (16.1 points lost), which dropped the lead to -23.2. Opus 5.5 then kept playing into the lower left, where moves 19 to 25 each lost 12.0 to 15.2 points, and the game ended at -25.8 on the board.", "moments": [{"turn": 15, "text": "H3 lost 10.0 points, swinging Black's lead from +2.4 to -7.6. The engine wanted D5, the point White took one move later. Black had just been handed a lead by White's 7.1-point slip at G2, and gave it straight back."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "G5 was the worst move of the game, losing 16.1 points and taking Black's lead from -7.1 to -23.2. The engine preferred C2. Black's stones on the right were already settled, and White's wall at C5, D5 and E5 above the lower-left stones was the real fight."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "C2 lost 12.1 points, taking Black from -25.9 to -38.0. By now the lower-left Black stones sat under the White wall with B3 and B4 added, and the engine would have played E7 elsewhere. White's B2 answer then gave back 12.4 points."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "E1 lost 15.2 points. Black was still adding stones to the bottom edge around D2 and E2 while the engine pointed to E7 in the open upper half. White's F1 reply threw away 15.3 points of its own, so the lead only moved from -40.7 to -25.4."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "White's C7 lost 3.5 points, one of the few real slips in a long quiet stretch where the lead hovered near -30. Black, with F8 next, was playing the engine's choice, but there was too little left on the board to matter, and Opus 5.5 resigned after White's B1."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The only program run was libs.py, which parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties for the current position; the other commands just read and appended to games.md and CLAUDE.md. None of it chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}